// expect: 7
// A USER'S NAME IS THE USER'S. `report` is a declaration of the compiler's
// src/types.mn, and until Landing 1 (2026-10-13) every program that imported
// io linked that module through one dead import line (lib/io.mn's `import
// types`), so this program was refused as a duplicate declaration — of a
// function the developer never heard of, in a file they never opened
// (E_DuplicateFnName on main's tree through boot 454c3aaf; the refusal is the
// library's, so the same boot over this tree's library runs it). The library
// imports nothing of the compiler now, and a user's reach never holds it.
import io

fn report(x) = x + 2

fn main() = {
  print_string("")
  report(5)
}
